 has $\\sigma - \\Re\\rho_1 < D$. For $\\tau$ near $\\Im \\rho_1$, a disk about $z = \\sigma + i\\tau$ of fixed radius less than $D$ contains $\\rho_1$, and for $\\tau$ in a short interval these disks meet only finitely many poles. Two poles with different imaginary parts are equidistant from $z$ for at most one $\\tau$; two with equal imaginary parts never are, as both lie left of $\\Re s = \\sigma$. Avoiding these finitely many $\\tau$, $z$ has a unique nearest pole $\\rho$, at distance $d < D$. Choose $d < r < D$ with $\\rho$ the only pole in $\\overline B(z, r)$. Since $\\overline B(\\sigma, r)$ has no pole and the residue $c$ is nonzero by \\hyperref[8JN4]{the lemma},\n\\[ |A_k(z)| + \\Re A_k(\\sigma) \\ge |c|\\, d^{-k-1} - O(r^{-k}). \\]\nMultiplying $(*)$ by $d^k$ and letting $k \\to \\infty$ gives $|c|/d \\le 0$.\n\n(b) Every pole has $\\sigma - \\Re\\rho \\ge D$. Applied to $\\rho_0$ this gives $D \\le \\sigma - \\Re\\rho_0 < D_*$, so $D = \\operatorname{dist}(\\sigma, Z)$, attained (as $Z$ is \\hyperref[8JS5]{locally finite}) at some $\\rho$ with\n\\[ |\\sigma - \\rho| = D \\le \\sigma - \\Re\\rho. \\]\nHence $\\rho = \\beta = \\sigma - D$ is real and the unique nearest pole, with residue $c_\\beta > 0$ by \\hyperref[8JS7]{the corollary}. For some $D < r < D_*$,\n\\[ \\Re A_k(\\sigma) = c_\\beta D^{-k-1} + O(r^{-k}), \\]\nwhile $(*)$ with $\\tau = 0$ gives $2\\Re A_k(\\sigma) \\le C_* D_*^{-k}$. Multiplying by $D^k$ gives $c_\\beta / D \\le 0$.\n\nBoth cases are impossible, so $\\Re\\rho \\le \\theta$ for all $\\rho \\in Z$. The positivity of the residue at real poles is what lets a \\emph{one-sided} bound exclude real zeros.","status":"ai_generated","generated_by":"claude","generator_detail":"claude-opus-5-5","reviewed_by":null,"review_notes":null,"position":1}', 'claude');
UPDATE proofs SET body_tex = 'Since $L(s,\chi) \ne 0$ for $\Re s \ge 1$ \cite{Davenport}, a real $\rho \in Z$ lies in $(0,1)$. By \ref{8JN4} and \ref{8JS5}(iii),
\[ \operatorname{Res}_{s=\rho} \mathcal H_\psi = \frac{S_\rho}{\rho(1-\rho)} > 0. \]', body_html_cache = NULL, revision = revision + 1, updated_at = '2026-11-24 15:30:00', updated_by = 'claude' WHERE id = 107;
INSERT INTO revisions (entity, entity_key, revision, operation_id, snapshot_json, author) VALUES ('proof', '107', 4, 'rename-Phi-to-calH-2026-11-24', '{"result_id":120,"body_tex":"Since $L(s,\\chi) \\ne 0$ for $\\Re s \\ge 1$ \\cite{Davenport}, a real $\\rho \\in Z$ lies in $(0,1)$. By \\ref{8JN4} and \\ref{8JS5}(iii),\n\\[ \\operatorname{Res}_{s=\\rho} \\mathcal H_\\psi = \\frac{S_\\rho}{\\rho(1-\\rho)} > 0. \\]","status":"ai_generated","generated_by":"claude","generator_detail":"claude-opus-5-5","reviewed_by":null,"review_notes":null,"position":1}', 'claude');
